  awschatapp-platform/ — Helm chart updates

  - templates/pdb.yaml — PodDisruptionBudget (toggle via pdb.enabled)
  - templates/networkpolicy.yaml — NetworkPolicy (toggle via networkPolicy.enabled)
  - templates/serviceaccount.yaml — references Terraform-managed SA
  - templates/api-deployment.yaml — pod + container securityContext blocks
  - values.yaml — new fields: serviceAccountName, securityContext, containerSecurityContext, pdb,
   networkPolicy

  Deployment flow after terraform apply

  cd chatappinfra
  terraform init
  # Bootstrap EKS first (Helm/k8s providers need the cluster)
  terraform apply -target=module.iam_bootstrap -target=module.vpc -target=module.kms
  -target=module.security_groups
  terraform apply -target=module.eks
  # Then everything else
  terraform apply

  # Deploy the app with the generated values file
  helm upgrade --install chatapp ../awschatapp-platform \
    --values ../awschatapp-platform/values.yaml \
    --values ../awschatapp-platform/values-prod-infra.yaml \
    -n chatapp --create-namespace

  Every production gap from the audit is addressed: HTTPS (ACM+ALB), RDS encryption + MySQL 8.0 +
   Multi-AZ + deletion protection, ElastiCache Multi-AZ + TLS, WAF, pod security context,
  NetworkPolicy, PDB, KMS etcd encryption, IRSA roles, Secrets Manager (no plaintext passwords),
  ALB access logs, and ALB idle timeout at 3600s for WebSockets.               